## DOCUMENTATION STRUCTURE

1. - `./documents/whiteboard.md`:
- Temporary notes
- Ongoing plans and progress marks.
- The only file for in-progress notes.

2. `./documents/project.md`
- Project overview, goals and requirements
- Problems solved and solutions provided
- Target audience and use cases
- Success metrics and constraints

3. `./documents/architecture.md`
- System architecture and layers
- Key design patterns and principles
- Component interactions
- Error handling and testing strategies

4. `./documents/implementation.md`
- Commands and their functionality (in table format)
- Technology stack and dependencies
- Development environment and setup

5. `./documents/file_structure.md`
- Complete file listing of the project
- Directory organization
- Key file purposes and relationships
- File organization patterns

6. `./documents/developer-manual.md`
- Developer manual for the project
- How to install dependencies
- How to run the project
- How to test the project
- How to build the project
- How to deploy the project

7. `./documents/user-manual.md`
- User manual for the project
- How to use the project
- How to test the project
- How to build the project
- How to deploy the project

8. `./**/README.md` - in all folders
- Notes about folder structure and file purposes
- Architecture decisions and design patterns on the folder level
- Key algorithms and data structures
- Performance considerations
- Error handling and testing strategies